  "chapter": {
    "number": 3,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          "And the Lord showed me Jesus the high priest standing before the angel of the Lord, and the",
          {
            "noteId": 1
          },
          "Devil stood on his right hand to resist him."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          "And the Lords said to the Devil,"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          "The Lord rebuke you, O Devil, even the Lord that has chosen Jerusalem rebuke you: behold! is not this as a brand plucked from the fire?"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          "Now Jesus was clothed in",
          {
            "noteId": 2
          },
          "filthy raiment, and stood before the angel."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          "And the Lord answered and spoke to those who stood before him, saying, Take away the filthy raiment from him: and he said to him, Behold, I have taken away your iniquities: and clothe you⌃ him with a",
          {
            "noteId": 3
          },
          "long robe,"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          "and place a pure mitre upon his head. So they placed a pure mitre upon his head, and clothed him with garments: and the angel of the Lord stood by."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          "And the angel of the Lord testified to Jesus, saying,"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          "Thus says the Lord Almighty; If you will walk in my ways, and take heed to my charges, then shall you judge my house: and if you will diligently keep my court, then will I give you men to walk in the midst of these that stand here."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          "Hear now, Jesus the high priest, you, and your neighbors that are sitting before you: for they are diviners, for, behold, I bring forth my servant The",
          {
            "noteId": 4
          },
          "Branch."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          "For as for the stone which I have set before the face of Jesus, on the one stone are seven eyes: behold, I am digging a trench, says the Lord Almighty, and I will search out all the iniquity of that land in one day."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          "In that day, says the Lord Almighty, you⌃ shall call together every man his neighbor under the vine and under the fig tree."
        ]
      }
    ],
